.TH FUSE 1 "November 2026" "Fuse" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fuse \- compose shaders, textures, and geometry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fuse gl
[\fB--builtins\fR | \fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fuse tex
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fuse mesh
[\fB--builtins\fR | \fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B fuse lsp
.br
.B fuse view
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--tex0\fR \fIFILE.ptex\fR] ... [\fB--tex3\fR \fIFILE.ptex\fR]
[\fB--texture-width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--texture-height\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR] \fIFILE.pgl|FILE.ptex\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fuse composes graphics from chained transformations. Compiler commands read
source from standard input, write output to standard output, and report
diagnostics on standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gl
Compile .pgl source to a GLSL 330 core fragment shader. Complete programs return
vec4. A rendering host supplies the fuseUv input, u_time and u_resolution
uniforms, and any used texture inputs tex0 through tex3.
.TP
.B tex
Evaluate .ptex source to an RGBA PNG image. Complete programs return vec4.
The default width and height are 256 pixels; the default noise seed is zero.
.TP
.B mesh
Evaluate .pmesh source to a Wavefront OBJ mesh. Complete programs return mesh.
.TP
.B lsp
Run the shared language server over JSON-RPC on standard input and output.
It provides diagnostics, receiver-aware completion, and hover for mixed
shader, texture, and geometry documents. A recognized language ID (fusegl,
fusetex, or fusemesh) selects the capability; otherwise the filename extension
is used. Unknown types receive a diagnostic and no completion or hover results.
.TP
.B view
Preview Fuse shader (.pgl) and texture (.ptex) source files with live reload. Supplies
time, resolution, and UV coordinates using an OpenGL 3.3 core context. Space
pauses or resumes animation; Escape closes the window. Errors go to standard
error and leave the last working shader and textures running. Bind procedural
texture sources with --tex0 through --tex3; each input reloads independently.
The default initial window size is 960 by 640. Press 1 for the shader or 2 through
5 for supplied tex0 through tex3 inputs. Switching preserves playback state.
The last show() call in each file selects its viewer output; normal compilation
treats show() as an identity function. An explicit --preview-line overrides
markers in the directly opened file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --builtins
Available on gl, tex, and mesh. Print the command's function signatures,
globals, and documentation.
.TP
.BI --preview-line " N"
Compile the intermediate result on a one-based source line. Shader and texture
previews accept numeric or vector values; geometry previews require a mesh.
.TP
.BI --width " N"
Set the texture width in pixels (tex), or initial window width (view).
.TP
.BI --height " N"
Set the texture height in pixels (tex), or initial window height (view).
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Set the unsigned noise seed (tex default: zero; view default: 42).
.TP
.BI --tex0 " FILE.ptex"
Bind a procedural texture source to tex0 (view). Also accepts --tex1, --tex2,
and --tex3. Paths are relative to the working directory.
.TP
.BI --texture-width " N"
Set generated texture width in pixels (view, default: 512).
.TP
.BI --texture-height " N"
Set generated texture height in pixels (view, default: 512).
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show available commands or help for a subcommand.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
fuse gl < shader.pgl > shader.frag
fuse tex --width 512 --height 512 --seed 42 < clouds.ptex > clouds.png
fuse mesh < disk.pmesh > disk.obj
fuse gl --preview-line 4 < shader.pgl > preview.frag
fuse view shader.pgl
fuse view clouds.ptex
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero for invalid commands, options, source,
or output. The viewer returns nonzero for startup failures; recoverable source
errors keep the window running. A selective build only provides its included
capabilities.
